  "step_2": "The individual states: 'Fast die selbe Wahrscheinlichkeit, daher habe ich mich für den höheren Gewinn entschieden.' This translates to: 'The probabilities are almost the same, therefore I chose the higher prize.' The individual acknowledges that the probabilities are nearly identical (33% vs. 34%), and bases the decision on the higher monetary outcome (2500 Euros vs. 2400 Euros). The deliberation process focuses on the similarity of probabilities and shifts the decision to the higher prize, without emphasizing or referencing the probability differences as a decisive factor. Thus, the individual does not appear to have used the probability-based reason (which prioritizes higher probability of favorable outcome) but instead uses the prize amount as the deciding factor, despite noting the probabilities are similar.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires that the individual consider the differences in probabilities and prefer the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome. However, in the verbal report, the individual downplays the probability difference, stating the probabilities are 'almost the same' and instead justifies the choice based on the higher prize. There is no mention of evaluating or prioritizing the probability of winning. Therefore, the individual did not apply the decision reason—instead, they used a different criterion (monetary value). The information relevant to the reason (probability differences) is acknowledged only minimally and not used in the justification. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
